# 20261005T015516-1001-192-168-30-104-26668.wav
#
# The start-up of a 14400 call modec placed through the bench, to five
# seconds past CONNECT, with what modec sent beside it (.sent).
#
# For the silence in the middle of it.  Figure 4 has the answering
# modem stop while the caller sends its conditioning signal, and with
# our own echo cancelled -- it is trained on to 28 dB in this call, in
# that very window -- the line carries nothing for two seconds.  A
# receiver that follows the line down has its gain up sixty decibels by
# the end of them; when the far end's second conditioning signal
# arrives, the timing detector, which divides by the level being
# tracked, puts out its limit until the gain comes back, and the symbol
# rate estimate is left 3700 ppm out.  On the call this recording is
# of, the second TRN was read at an error of 0.2, E was missed, and the
# data pump opened on a line it could not read and asked for a retrain
# three seconds later -- which is the retrain this fixture's ceiling of
# none is here to catch.  Held through the silence
# ('Modec.QAM.qrFadeHold'), the receiver reads 27 to 31 dB from the
# first data symbol.
#
# No bytes: the far end idles for the whole of what is kept.  It
# retrains at 23.7 s, answering the request the live call made, and the
# recording stops short of that.
seconds:   23.4
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis
v8:        no
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
tolerance: 0
